{\n  \"pdf-tools\": {\n    \"title\": \"PDF Tools\",\n    \"description\": \"Merge, compress, split, protect, reorder, and convert PDF documents online. All tools run 100% locally in your browser memory for absolute file safety.\",\n    \"intro_h2\": \"Ultimate PDF Manipulation and Optimization Hub\",\n    \"introduction\": \"Welcome to the ToolTari PDF Tools category hub. The Portable Document Format (PDF) has become the global standard for business, legal, and academic document exchange. However, modifying these files traditionally required expensive licenses or uploading confidential papers to remote servers, exposing private data to security breaches. ToolTari solves this by offering a complete suite of browser-native PDF utilities. Whether you need to merge digital contracts, compress heavy file sizes under 2MB for portal uploads, split pages, protect files with password layers, or convert PDFs to editable formats, everything runs client-side. Using modern JavaScript libraries and WebAssembly sandboxes, your document files are parsed and compiled in local volatile memory, keeping your data 100% secure and private.\",\n    \"beginner_guide_title\": \"Beginner: Working with Portable Document Formats\",\n    \"beginner_guide_text\": \"PDF is a fixed-layout file format designed to preserve exact visual alignment, fonts, and graphics across all platforms. Unlike Word files which change layout depending on screen size or operating system, PDFs look identical on a phone, laptop, or paper. To start, simply select a tool, drop your document into our drag-and-drop zone, apply options, and download the output. There is no signup required, and no watermarks are added.\",\n    \"advanced_guide_title\": \"Advanced: PDF Objects Dictionary & Structure\",\n    \"advanced_guide_text\": \"A PDF file is structured as a hierarchical catalog of objects (dictionary) mapping page arrays, content streams, fonts, annotations, and outlines. When ToolTari merges or splits PDFs, the client-side compiler reads this cross-reference (xref